31,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems that users are most satisfied when spaces are bookable by any department, whereas single-wing benefits are rated poorly. Also, general-purpose rooms are in high demand year-round.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"I've found that every room taken out of service for works requires expensive off-site hired space, and I agree with Mizuki that general-purpose rooms are constantly overbooked.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender records show a significant rise in costs for mechanical and ducted plant, while the delivery schedules reveal that projects based on comfort or appeal often slip by a year or more.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I also saw those rising costs in the tenders, and it turns out there's no renewal reserve for old audiovisual kit, even though it's been written down!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My findings show that while front-of-house and grounds posts remain unfilled, bench technicians are wasting hours every week on manual checks because the current extraction equipment is inadequate.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that sounds like a serious inefficiency. If the equipment is failing the staff, it seems like a priority.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree, but we must consider the cost of off-site space if we take rooms out of service for such upgrades.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a valid point, though we must also weigh that against Benjamin's finding that mechanical plant costs are rising; delaying only makes the eventual bill higher.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, Benjamin just talked about himself in the third person! But he's right—if costs are going up, we should probably act now before it gets even more expensive.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. The technicians are struggling with outdated systems, and as Benjamin noted, the cost of mechanical upgrades is only climbing. We can't ignore the human cost of this inefficiency.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we prioritize the technicians' needs, we should ensure the solution doesn't just benefit one wing, as my data suggests that's where satisfaction drops.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that is a fair point, but if the ventilation is a critical failure, the utility to the staff might outweigh the general booking satisfaction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, but we must also be wary of the delivery schedules; if we propose a project based on ""comfort,"" we risk a year-long delay. We need a rationale that ensures timely completion.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,Maybe we can frame the ventilation as a necessity rather than just comfort? That way it won't slip on the schedule like Benjamin said!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Precisely, Kenji. This isn't about comfort; it's about operational failure and staff burnout. It's a necessity that should bypass the typical delays associated with ""appeal"" projects.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with that framing. If we can address the operational failure while ensuring the project is seen as a necessity, it aligns with both the staff's needs and the delivery data.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I still worry about the off-site hiring costs, but if the current system is truly failing the technicians, the risk of inaction seems higher.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a consensus on the urgency. If we can justify the project as a critical infrastructure requirement, we mitigate both the cost and schedule risks.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm all for it! Let's make sure we pick the plan that fixes those ventilation problems and helps the technicians out.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I believe we are all in agreement then. Let's move to the final selection and ensure the technicians finally get the relief they deserve.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
