56,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Now that the candidates are listed, it's clear that Candidate D, the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade, directly addresses the operational failures and technician burdens Shunichi identified.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree; Candidate D is the only one that solves the critical equipment issues, though we must be mindful of the room displacement costs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate D is the most logical choice, as it frames the work as a critical infrastructure necessity, which should help avoid the scheduling slips I noted.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate D is definitely the way to go! It fixes the ventilation and helps the technicians, and it's way better than just adding more study space.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,I couldn't agree more. Candidate D is the only option that provides the necessary relief for our staff and fixes a failing system.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Since we are all in agreement on the rationale and the urgency, I see no reason to debate the other candidates further.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I concur. The evidence regarding staff burden and rising mechanical costs makes Candidate D the most rational priority for this budget cycle.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. Given the data we've reviewed, any other choice would be an inefficient use of resources and a failure to address a systemic risk.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally on board! Let's just go ahead and vote for Candidate D so we can get those technicians some help!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,It is settled then. I will cast my vote for Candidate D to ensure our staff are no longer burdened by obsolete equipment.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I will also vote for Candidate D, as it is the most responsible choice for the university's operational health.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I vote for Candidate D, as the necessity of the upgrade outweighs the temporary displacement costs.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I cast my vote for Candidate D, as it is the only option that aligns with both the financial and scheduling data.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote for Candidate D! Let's get this project started and help the staff!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
